    "text": "Complex A has a composition of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>12</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi></math>. If the complex on treatment with conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> loses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;of its original mass, the correct molecular formulas of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is:<br />[Given : atomic mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>52</mn></math>&nbsp;amu and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math>amu]",
